repository-code: https://github.com/AkshatTm/SIH-PS143
abstract: >-
  Naap detects oil slicks in Sentinel-1 SAR imagery, separates them from
  look-alikes, runs ocean-current and wind physics backwards in time to
  reconstruct a probability cloud for where and when the oil entered the
  water, and scores broadcasting vessels, dark vessels and fixed
  infrastructure against that cloud to produce a ranked, explainable
  shortlist with explicit exclusions and an abstain option. A fourth stage
  compares each conclusion against the official investigation of record and
  reports hit, partial or miss. Built for Smart India Hackathon 2026,
  problem statement 26143 (NTRO). The system ships as a library of nine
  reproducible case bundles; every reported figure carries its measurement
  method, sample size and split.
keywords:
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - Sentinel-1
  - oil spill detection
  - source attribution
  - maritime domain awareness
  - AIS
  - dark vessels
  - Lagrangian backtracking
  - remote sensing
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
date-released: '2026-09-14'
